    </span><span class="unknown token" data-binding>∀</span><span class="inter-text"> </span><span class="var token" data-binding="var-_uniq.53660" data-verso-hover="3">i</span><span class="inter-text"> </span><span class="punctuation bracket token" data-binding="kw-occ-Lean.Parser.Term.explicitBinder-3348">(</span><span class="wildcard token" data-binding>_</span><span class="inter-text"> </span><span class="built-in delim token" data-binding="kw-occ-Lean.Parser.Term.explicitBinder-3348">:</span><span class="inter-text"> </span><span class="var token" data-binding="var-_uniq.53530" data-verso-hover="3">lo</span><span class="inter-text"> </span><span class="punctuation operator token" data-binding="kw-occ-«term_≤_»-3353">≤</span><span class="inter-text"> </span><span class="var token" data-binding="var-_uniq.53660" data-verso-hover="3">i</span><span class="punctuation bracket token" data-binding="kw-occ-Lean.Parser.Term.explicitBinder-3348">)</span><span class="inter-text"> </span><span class="punctuation bracket token" data-binding="kw-occ-Lean.Parser.Term.explicitBinder-3363">(</span><span class="wildcard token" data-binding>_</span><span class="inter-text"> </span><span class="built-in delim token" data-binding="kw-occ-Lean.Parser.Term.explicitBinder-3363">:</span><span class="inter-text"> </span><span class="var token" data-binding="var-_uniq.53660" data-verso-hover="3">i</span><span class="inter-text"> </span><span class="punctuation operator token" data-binding="kw-occ-«term_<_»-3368">&lt;</span><span class="inter-text"> </span><span class="var token" data-binding="var-_uniq.53533" data-verso-hover="3">hi</span><span class="punctuation bracket token" data-binding="kw-occ-Lean.Parser.Term.explicitBinder-3363">)</span><span class="punctuation separator token" data-binding="kw-occ-Lean.Parser.Term.forall-3342">,</span><span class="inter-text"> </span><span class="var token" data-binding="var-_uniq.53524" data-verso-hover="46">a</span><span class="punctuation bracket token" data-binding="kw-occ-«term__[_]»-3377">[</span><span class="var token" data-binding="var-_uniq.53660" data-verso-hover="3">i</span><span class="punctuation bracket token" data-binding="kw-occ-«term__[_]»-3377">]</span><span class="inter-text"> </span><span class="punctuation operator token" data-binding="kw-occ-«term_≠_»-3377">≠</span><span class="inter-text"> </span><span class="var token" data-binding="var-_uniq.53527" data-verso-hover="49">x</span><span class="inter-text"> </span><span class="built-in delim token" data-binding="kw-occ-Lean.Parser.Command.declValSimple-3388">:=</span><span class="inter-text"> </span><span class="keyword token" data-binding="kw-occ-Lean.Parser.Term.byTactic-3391" data-verso-hover="8">by</span><span class="inter-text">
  </span><span class="keyword token" data-binding="kw-occ-Lean.Parser.Tactic.funInduction-3396" data-verso-hover="65">fun_induction</span><span class="inter-text"> </span><span class="const token" data-binding="const-bsearch" data-verso-hover="45">bsearch</span><span class="inter-text"> </span><span class="unknown token" data-binding>&lt;;&gt;</span><span class="inter-text">
    </span><span class="keyword token" data-binding="kw-occ-Lean.Parser.Tactic.grind-3426" data-verso-hover="10">grind</span><span class="inter-text"> </span><span class="punctuation bracket token" data-binding="kw-occ-Lean.Parser.Tactic.grind-3426">[</span><span class="const token" data-binding="const-List.pairwise_iff_getElem" data-verso-hover="66">List.pairwise_iff_getElem</span><span class="punctuation bracket token" data-binding="kw-occ-Lean.Parser.Tactic.grind-3426">]</span></code></div></div><div class="code-gallery-footer"><div class="code-gallery-footer-left"><div class="code-gallery-tip active"><span><p>Grind is a powerful tool that can help you prove theorems quickly and efficiently.</p></span><a class="code-gallery-run" href="https://live.lean-lang.org/#codez=JYWwDg9gTgLgBAZRgEwFCoPQFotwJIB2yArgMYzAQFwCGRiAsgCpYA2wA1gKZxRc0BnKsAIBzOMQEjxAA1FQRyGXCwZUMABZdoXEHFHaQXGAtIB9AVwUCLxPQAoAHnABc%2BAjACUce9TcA5Gi9XVDgwn2dcAEZvACofewAZYAEYADooOgM4Ak80kBowCLgAPTgAds88gTtQ8LCAXjhnMupo1yaAIwBPOsUyCiocuAAeAG4APn0FegBtZNSMrK5bUlIAXXRsXBpWA07M4FJefiECaTgRCSkxODkZpRU1TW0%2BPS5iVisbADMIYigFgAjsQaHwzMBkFwPMAYN0fDQ4J04MdkHAikDeHABK53MEXHUwvYaCUAExwADUSLJlJRNKpyDJcR8YHpcCBbKgbIETLgDUJ4WJsSKuE6sUxuFIsSgKjgyFiAk8bKFmKpYqKVKlONw8qgStJArCVKFMtFCtpUo1cvF%2BsNtKFOLV0tlUtV1rA%2Bo6SN6YXkii2ODunQAbmYoaRIVwBMpw5GcZ1YcGuORoHAuCCgpQCNrnlodHpIAB3KxmCA%2FMwwQsQMwJmAVqPwJy4gBCsIAasm4AA2AAs3gJ9SbAEImgAGOAAMgnzUnU%2BK0W8DTHi4iaVIkCKS7gMS9PTqIbDycjQA&amp;challengez=C4Cwpg9gTmC2AEYCuAbMUDOB9AZhJUWGAjkgIYxYCWAJmAHbBXACe8AFGfAEbwDG8GvAAO8YvCjwM8AFzwAkowCUsgFDwNHMgD0ATPADUPPYf4mjNPSoBUHYebEOoDjFfgBedZo2drogLQ81uKBfNaSgTTWGEoOvuJG3H6mYdKR4bG6Xt5GvhFB0kZhohbBmdmauWTRpkn5YQmCfpmy7jwsXhjQUB1AA"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="25px" height="25px" fill="#386EE0"><g data-name="Layer 2"><g data-name="arrow-right"><rect width="24" height="24" transform="rotate(180 12 12)" opacity="0"></rect><path d="M10.46 18a2.23 2.23 0 0 1-.91-.2 1.76 1.76 0 0 1-1.05-1.59V7.79A1.76 1.76 0 0 1 9.55 6.2a2.1 2.1 0 0 1 2.21.26l5.1 4.21a1.7 1.7 0 0 1 0 2.66l-5.1 4.21a2.06 2.06 0 0 1-1.3.46zm0-10v7.9l4.86-3.9z"></path></g></g></svg></a></div><div class="code-gallery-tip"><span><p>Build a formal argument one tactic at a time and let Lean track every remaining goal.</p></span><a class="code-gallery-run" href="https://live.lean-lang.org/#codez=PQWhAIEFwBwJwJYFsCm4EGdwENwDsBXJAIxTnABts4BzM8AFwAts9wBGcAdwWfAHs8FAJ6NEANwTYK4ACYJJGfnCwhgAKFkoAZuACSGAAqJU4ABRsAXOABy2BgEpwlgLwdwAHnzhA5EThAAETgANYANO5eQeCASYTBnt4xADWxgMRE%2BOrqoBAAouJkooQk9FS09Mys7ixYuPDIaNrYAMYMyuBq6swoyihI4CgAHpgMGAD6NajD9U0tlurgcwH4YZxebDGAwETBYQbGtbF%2BkalWbsTCs%2Bh4DHD83kzsZ2DgWbxM9AAGeK%2FoWGMoAHT%2FZxOwwa2AwKCwTB%2Bzn0RhMaDwZwA7eAaIg8LJwABtOwMX6ycSyYZwHQUAC69wg%2F1%2BAnIvHAlRw%2BEEIEuCikMnkihaPD41Th4EmzTgSIExAY2AQbEAF%2BShcDDQCX5NCNrLlntYitfClvK5wCczvNwBhkDBhtIZJjtnDyQb%2BGKJdKYGFhk7FTr%2BoMRj8Jo0hbEzCcUWjZA59YHJRjsfY8QThpdWBhyRkHgAVF4Cn3KdlhLTaSUoDHEhoEFQKFAiMI8pjgIsYZo9PD8cUMBCCVoaHPpqaIaTQnHRWz2M4AH3AAAZwC4AHwcYf4ADUnCn5jYc44TgAVJ2hey0g2my28JZ2KOT%%2BBk%2BV2KDKGoOhyDKNhRvUNpROJHo9DwMreK0AB5bQdlQLBpKUjYYHAacEJhW60GerT0POLC0jmFgQOsVU2EW9xvrDKywpghMzltcVJXAKVHXpFGFVQ3oBlrT04W9Ltl3AMH2CcZhMDODACG0XMGnBcAEmexS2ADSzZDOTC9LMYZoQZ%2FAQwB7AgfCWAMchX47n5wXnsOQmMdsvHt0fYXAE4CHm8EALgJzGZoM%2BfpAW0B1Dy5Yp4hwBV8BpaJjWzYttWzhZrEPOwWRCWN4FWBpxzfO0NyBxsmNBBQUkgA&amp;challengez=CYUwZgBAkgzgCgJwJYFsQQBQDsIC4IByAhgC4CUeAvBAIwQA8EOg5EQSAARBANYA0tDXEQEmEAxjmEAagYGIiJgChZJABYgA9ghApoWMEixISAV1AB5MIlQgYedk16BgIggAHCAD5b0eMjROqEAEYAnrIQEDBqCAFAA"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="25px" height="25px" fill="#386EE0"><g data-name="Layer 2"><g data-name="arrow-right"><rect width="24" height="24" transform="rotate(180 12 12)" opacity="0"></rect><path d="M10.46 18a2.23 2.23 0 0 1-.91-.2 1.76 1.76 0 0 1-1.05-1.59V7.79A1.76 1.76 0 0 1 9.55 6.2a2.1 2.1 0 0 1 2.21.26l5.1 4.21a1.7 1.7 0 0 1 0 2.66l-5.1 4.21a2.06 2.06 0 0 1-1.3.46zm0-10v7.9l4.86-3.9z"></path></g></g></svg></a></div><div class="code-gallery-tip"><span><p>Index safety, termination and correctness are all checked by Lean, so off-by-one bugs never compile.</p></span><a class="code-gallery-run" href="https://live.lean-lang.org/#codez=PQWhAIFEDcFMCcCe4CGBtAtgXXASwM7gAO8A9nAHZ5UBGpArhQCaEoAu4AxqRkbgDaxwbXBlgAoAEqxO9ePlwUA5uFJUABhnXV8bWCiaqAZuE3gA1OACM2%2FqVJFCR0vFhx4AGlTNwAGX1UrgBWMmyEuGziIMDiTLAmNPj68JwAFuAAFCjgAFzgAILw8CjIAKoAkhRsAGwALACUmQAeueAVVXWNGXbgqbitAHLs9eLgY5npeX3ggCZEqAB0CgBesI15APJEImrgQxw5ALyjeCYA%2Bq09ADy9%2FWypsBTHY4IcGLkH4D2WGdMQdo3AcAAJieJ1QmBw1xadwe4ESyTSqHALQyb0sVka01SoNg%2FCSYJa13Q2GE91oSRQKXS2RaPTeGRoyH4uBQI3G4Fx%2BPwPCEGGOnKEFDUEj08AwinYuDUp0ZN3Af1I4nEoAg6yo3PgekMiiI9DYXnUQoosG0YhQFEILVcKH4%2FGQBFQ8KqOXEQuMRhAjJAwq45vA%2BAA1rgiKp3HhItFxDCXLA3vDKWlTkahFlWoVimVKjUGs1PqQ5ak2eMMhqta0UPM2KRfAQ2PMAAooXDwADuBBTAHbZuAO%2FUi2MflQ8vGqUjafmseAPsm1qDAABEeEy5zyPTmuC6y8X1z69S86FwOEABkTI95wxDHIyMU6KJj0TjbckI9KXADcAD5QUp4DfwGga7p5iIJtW3ba8jCMU4lFgNhIEEbAgA"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="25px" height="25px" fill="#386EE0"><g data-name="Layer 2"><g data-name="arrow-right"><rect width="24" height="24" transform="rotate(180 12 12)" opacity="0"></rect><path d="M10.46 18a2.23 2.23 0 0 1-.91-.2 1.76 1.76 0 0 1-1.05-1.59V7.79A1.76 1.76 0 0 1 9.55 6.2a2.1 2.1 0 0 1 2.21.26l5.1 4.21a1.7 1.7 0 0 1 0 2.66l-5.1 4.21a2.06 2.06 0 0 1-1.3.46zm0-10v7.9l4.86-3.9z"></path></g></g></svg></a></div></div></div></div></div></div><section class="hero-bottom card reveal transition-delay-xl" aria-label="Advantages of Lean"><article class="feature"><header class="feature-title"><figure class="feature-icon"><img src="/static/svg/home/trustworthy.svg" alt aria-hidden="true"/></figure><h3 class="feature-text">Trustworthy</h3></header><p class="feature-description">Lean's minimal trusted kernel guarantees absolute correctness in mathematical proof, software and hardware verification.</p></article><article class="feature"><header class="feature-title"><figure class="feature-icon"><img src="/static/svg/home/powerful.svg" alt aria-hidden="true"/></figure><h3 class="feature-text">Powerful</h3></header><p class="feature-description">From elementary concepts to cutting-edge research, Lean's expressive language and extensive built-in tools let users focus on the big picture rather than routine details.</p></article><article class="feature"><header class="feature-title"><figure class="feature-icon"><img src="/static/svg/home/extensible.svg" alt aria-hidden="true"/></figure><h3 class="feature-text">Extensible</h3></header><p class="feature-description">Lean's metaprogramming capabilities enable users to extend the language with domain-specific notations and new proof automation techniques.</p></article></section></div></section><section class="projects-section section-container container reveal" id="lean-in-action" aria-label="Lean in Action"><div class="heading-section"><span class="badge-primary">USE CASES</span><h1 class="heading-title">Lean in <span>Action</span></h1><p class="heading-subtitle">Showcasing real-world applications.</p></div><div class="projects-layout"><aside class="project-index" aria-label="Featured projects"><nav class="project-index-list project-accordion" aria-label="Choose a featured project"><section class="project-accordion-item active" data-project="mathlib"><button id="project-trigger-mathlib" type="button" class="project-index-button active" data-project="mathlib" aria-controls="project-summary-mathlib" aria-expanded="true"><span>Mathlib</span><span class="project-accordion-indicator" aria-hidden="true"></span></button><div class="project-index-panel-wrap"><article id="project-summary-mathlib" class="project-index-panel" data-project="mathlib" aria-labelledby="project-trigger-mathlib" aria-hidden="false"><p>Mathlib is Lean's comprehensive mathematical library containing over a million lines of formalized mathematics spanning algebra, analysis, topology, probability, and computer science. This community-driven resource enables mathematicians to tackle frontier research problems and engineers to build verified systems by providing a rigorously verified foundation of mathematical knowledge that eliminates duplication of effort.</p><a href="/use-cases/mathlib">Explore Project →</a></article></div></section><section class="project-accordion-item" data-project="aeneas"><button id="project-trigger-aeneas" type="button" class="project-index-button" data-project="aeneas" aria-controls="project-summary-aeneas" aria-expanded="false"><span>Aeneas</span><span class="project-accordion-indicator" aria-hidden="true"></span></button><div class="project-index-panel-wrap"><article id="project-summary-aeneas" class="project-index-panel" data-project="aeneas" aria-labelledby="project-trigger-aeneas" aria-hidden="true"><p>Aeneas takes a novel approach to Rust verification. Unlike other verification approaches that must reason about memory directly, Aeneas leverages Rust's rich type system to eliminate memory reasoning entirely for many Rust programs.</p><a href="/use-cases/aeneas">Explore Project →</a></article></div></section><section class="project-accordion-item" data-project="cedar"><button id="project-trigger-cedar" type="button" class="project-index-button" data-project="cedar" aria-controls="project-summary-cedar" aria-expanded="false"><span>Cedar</span><span class="project-accordion-indicator" aria-hidden="true"></span></button><div class="project-index-panel-wrap"><article id="project-summary-cedar" class="project-index-panel" data-project="cedar" aria-labelledby="project-trigger-cedar" aria-hidden="true"><p>AWS uses Lean and verification-guided development to formally verify Cedar, the AWS authorization policy language. The approach involves creating executable models in Lean, proving security properties, and validating them against production code through differential testing. This achieves high assurance with minimal runtime overhead, demonstrating Lean's viability for verifying critical software.</p><a href="/use-cases/cedar">Explore Project →</a></article></div></section></nav></aside><div class="project-gallery"><a id="project-gallery-mathlib" class="project-gallery-card" data-project="mathlib" href="/use-cases/mathlib"><span class="project-gallery-media"><img src="/static/png/mathlib.png" alt="Image of a grid with the LEAN logo with Mathlib below." loading="lazy"/><span class="project-gallery-shade" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="project-gallery-copy"><strong>Mathlib</strong><span>The community mathematics library</span></span></span><span class="project-gallery-detail"><span class="project-gallery-description">Mathlib is Lean's comprehensive mathematical library containing over a million lines of formalized mathematics spanning algebra, analysis, topology, probability, and computer science. This community-driven resource enables mathematicians to tackle frontier research problems and engineers to build verified systems by providing a rigorously verified foundation of mathematical knowledge that eliminates duplication of effort.</span><span class="project-gallery-cta">Explore Project →</span></span></a><a id="project-gallery-aeneas" class="project-gallery-card" data-project="aeneas" href="/use-cases/aeneas"><span class="project-gallery-media"><img src="/static/png/aeneas.png" alt="Aeneas (the greek mythology character) hurt by an arrow, with a finger in the head" loading="lazy"/><span class="project-gallery-shade" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="project-gallery-copy"><strong>Aeneas</strong><span>Verified Rust</span></span></span><span class="project-gallery-detail"><span class="project-gallery-description">Aeneas takes a novel approach to Rust verification. Unlike other verification approaches that must reason about memory directly, Aeneas leverages Rust's rich type system to eliminate memory reasoning entirely for many Rust programs.</span><span class="project-gallery-cta">Explore Project →</span></span></a><a id="project-gallery-cedar" class="project-gallery-card" data-project="cedar" href="/use-cases/cedar"><span class="project-gallery-media"><img src="/static/png/cedar.png" alt="A green background with a stylized cedar tree image and the word cedar" loading="lazy"/><span class="project-gallery-shade" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="project-gallery-copy"><strong>Cedar</strong><span>Verified authorization policies</span></span></span><span class="project-gallery-detail"><span class="project-gallery-description">AWS uses Lean and verification-guided development to formally verify Cedar, the AWS authorization policy language. The approach involves creating executable models in Lean, proving security properties, and validating them against production code through differential testing. This achieves high assurance with minimal runtime overhead, demonstrating Lean's viability for verifying critical software.</span><span class="project-gallery-cta">Explore Project →</span></span></a></div></div></section><section class="other-projects section-container container reveal" aria-label="More from the Lean ecosystem"><header class="other-projects-header"><span class="other-projects-eyebrow">MORE FROM THE LEAN ECOSYSTEM</span><span class="other-projects-divider" aria-hidden="true"></span></header><div class="other-projects-grid"><article class="other-project-card"><div class="other-project-image"><img src="/static/png/tauceti.png" alt="The Tau Ceti logo" loading="lazy"/></div><div class="other-project-content"><h3 class="other-project-title">Tau Ceti</h3><p class="other-project-description">Tau Ceti uses AI to build a reusable library of formalized mathematics on top of Mathlib. Humans direct the work through curated roadmaps, AI contributors write and review the code, and Lean's kernel checks the proofs. Recent results include Burnside's theorem, Carathéodory's boundary extension theorem, and Schur–Weyl duality. The goal is to provide the foundations researchers need to reach the mathematical research frontier.</p><a href="/use-cases/tau-ceti" class="read-more">Read more<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20px" height="20px" fill="#000"><g data-name="Layer 2"><g data-name="arrow-forward"><rect width="24" height="24" transform="rotate(-90 12 12)" opacity="0"></rect><path d="M5 13h11.86l-3.63 4.36a1 1 0 0 0 1.54 1.28l5-6a1.19 1.19 0 0 0 .09-.15c0-.05.05-.08.07-.13A1 1 0 0 0 20 12a1 1 0 0 0-.07-.36c0-.05-.05-.08-.07-.13a1.19 1.19 0 0 0-.09-.15l-5-6A1 1 0 0 0 14 5a1 1 0 0 0-.64.23 1 1 0 0 0-.13 1.41L16.86 11H5a1 1 0 0 0 0 2z"></path></g></g></svg></a></div></article><article class="other-project-card"><div class="other-project-image"><img src="/static/png/fermat.png" alt="Pierre de Fermat painting by Rolland Lefebvre" loading="lazy"/></div><div class="other-project-content"><h3 class="other-project-title">Fermat's Last Theorem</h3><p class="other-project-description">The Fermat's Last Theorem project is formalizing one of mathematics' most complex proofs in Lean, demonstrating the proof assistant's capacity to handle frontier research mathematics. This ambitious work is creating formalized definitions for advanced number-theoretic objects, enabling mathematicians to build machine-verified proofs of cutting-edge results while establishing Lean as a powerful platform for mathematical collaboration.</p><a href="/use-cases/flt" class="read-more">Read more<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="20px" height="20px" fill="#000"><g data-name="Layer 2"><g data-name="arrow-forward"><rect width="24" height="24" transform="rotate(-90 12 12)" opacity="0"></rect><path d="M5 13h11.86l-3.63 4.36a1 1 0 0 0 1.54 1.28l5-6a1.19 1.19 0 0 0 .09-.15c0-.05.05-.08.07-.13A1 1 0 0 0 20 12a1 1 0 0 0-.07-.36c0-.05-.05-.08-.07-.13a1.19 1.19 0 0 0-.09-.15l-5-6A1 1 0 0 0 14 5a1 1 0 0 0-.64.23 1 1 0 0 0-.13 1.41L16.86 11H5a1 1 0 0 0 0 2z"></path></g></g></svg></a></div></article><article class="other-project-card other-project-cta"><div class="other-project-cta-content"><span class="other-project-cta-eyebrow">USE CASES</span><h3 class="other-project-cta-title">Browse the full gallery</h3><p class="other-project-cta-description">See how engineering teams and research labs are putting Lean to work.</p></div><a href="/use-cases" class="other-project-cta-button">Explore All Use Cases</a></article></div></section><section class="testimonials-section" id="testimonials" aria-label="From our Community"><div class="testimonials-inner container"><header class="testimonials-heading reveal"><span class="testimonials-eyebrow">COMMUNITY</span><h2>From our <span>Community</span></h2><p>Voices from the people formalizing math and verifying software with Lean.</p></header><div class="testimonials-grid reveal transition-delay-small"><figure class="testimonial-card"><blockquote>Lean enables large-scale collaboration by allowing mathematicians to break down complex proofs into smaller, verifiable components […] With Lean, we are beginning to see how AI can accelerate the formalization of mathematics, opening up new possibilities for research.</blockquote><figcaption class="testimonial-author"><span class="testimonial-name">Terence Tao</span><span class="testimonial-role">Mathematician, UCLA</span></figcaption></figure><figure class="testimonial-card testimonial-card--tinted"><blockquote>Mathematical Superintelligence (MSI) with Lean will play a critical role in any industry where safety is paramount, including aerospace, automotive, and medical technology.</blockquote><figcaption class="testimonial-author"><span class="testimonial-name">Tudor Achim</span><span class="testimonial-role">Co-Founder and CEO, Harmonic</span></figcaption></figure><figure class="testimonial-card testimonial-card--filled"><blockquote>At Google DeepMind, we used Lean to build AlphaProof, a new reinforcement-learning based system for formal math reasoning. Lean’s extensibility and verification capabilities were key in enabling the development of AlphaProof.</blockquote><figcaption class="testimonial-author"><span class="testimonial-name">Pushmeet Kohli</span><span class="testimonial-role">VP, Science and Strategic Initiatives, Google DeepMind</span></figcaption></figure><figure class="testimonial-card"><blockquote>Lean has become a key enabler in scaling automated reasoning at Amazon. Its capacity to verify complex systems involving advanced mathematical concepts has transformed how we tackle problems once thought too complex or impractical. Lean is an indispensable tool in modern, large-scale software engineering, helping ensure soundness, correctness, and verified AI across our systems.</blockquote><figcaption class="testimonial-author"><span class="testimonial-name">Byron Cook</span><span class="testimonial-role">VP and Distinguished Scientist, AWS</span></figcaption></figure><figure class="testimonial-card"><blockquote>Lean is the core verification technology behind Cedar, the open-source authorization language that powers cloud services like Amazon Verified Permissions and AWS Verified Access […] Lean’s efficiency, extensive libraries, and vibrant community enable us to develop and maintain Cedar at scale, while ensuring the key correctness and security properties that our users depend on.</blockquote><figcaption class="testimonial-author"><span class="testimonial-name">Emina Torlak</span><span class="testimonial-role">Senior Principal Applied Scientist, AWS</span></figcaption></figure></div></div></section><section id="for-developers" class="code-feature code-feature--developers" aria-label="FOR DEVELOPERS"><div class="code-feature-inner container"><header class="code-feature-heading reveal"><span class="code-feature-eyebrow">FOR DEVELOPERS</span><h2>Write software. <span class="code-feature-emphasis">Prove it correct.</span></h2><p>Lean is a real functional language that compiles to native code. Its dependent type system lets you write a precise specification, then prove your software meets it.</p></header><div class="code-feature-layout reveal transition-delay-small"><div class="code-feature-details"><div class="code-feature-items"><article class="code-feature-item"><header class="code-feature-item-header"><span class="code-feature-marker"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="8" cy="8" r="6.2"></circle><path d="M5.6 8.2l1.7 1.7 3.3-3.8"></path></svg></span><h3>Covers every case</h3></header><p>A single proof guarantees correctness for every possible input a function could receive, not just the tested examples.</p></article><article class="code-feature-item"><header class="code-feature-item-header"><span class="code-feature-marker"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 4.8L2.6 8 6 11.2"></path><path d="M10 4.8L13.4 8 10 11.2"></path></svg></span><h3>Proofs live with your code</h3></header><p>There's no separate spec language. You write proofs in the same language you write your program in.</p></article></div><nav class="code-feature-links" aria-label="FOR DEVELOPERS resources"><a class="code-feature-link code-feature-link--primary" href="/getting-started">Get Started</a><a class="code-feature-link" href="https://lean-lang.org/functional_programming_in_lean/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read: Functional Programming in Lean</a></nav></div><div class="code-feature-code"><div class="lean-themed vscode-frame"><div class="vscode-titlebar"><p class="vscode-title">Service.lean</p></div><div class="vscode-workspace"><div class="vscode-editor" aria-label="Editor: Service.lean"><div class="code-gallery-box code-gallery-box--editor"><div class="code-gallery-tabs" role="tablist"><div class="code-gallery-tab active" role="tab" aria-selected="true"><p>Service.lean</p></div><div class="code-gallery-tab filler"></div><div class