3>Automate routine steps</h3></header><p>Use more powerful tactics to combine many elementary steps into one, so you spend less time on routine reasoning.</p></article><article class="code-feature-item"><header class="code-feature-item-header"><span class="code-feature-marker"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 8h2.8l1.9-4.2 2.6 8.4 1.8-4.2H14"></path></svg></span><h3>Real-time feedback as you write</h3></header><p>Lean's Infoview shows your current goal and hypotheses live, updating with every tactic so you always know what's left to prove.</p></article></div><nav class="code-feature-links" aria-label="FOR MATHEMATICIANS resources"><a class="code-feature-link code-feature-link--primary" href="/getting-started">Get Started</a><a class="code-feature-link" href="https://lean-lang.org/theorem_proving_in_lean4/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read: Theorem Proving in Lean</a></nav></div><div class="code-feature-code"><div class="lean-themed vscode-frame"><div class="vscode-titlebar"><p class="vscode-title">Infinitude.lean</p></div><div class="vscode-workspace"><div class="vscode-editor" aria-label="Editor: Infinitude.lean"><div class="code-gallery-box code-gallery-box--editor"><div class="code-gallery-tabs" role="tablist"><div class="code-gallery-tab active" role="tab" aria-selected="true"><p>InfinitudeOfPrimes.lean</p></div><div class="code-gallery-tab filler"></div><div class="code-gallery-tab-border"></div></div><div class="code-gallery-content" tabindex="-1"><div class="code-gallery-snippet visible-code"><div class="lean-preamble-group"><div class="lean-preamble" hidden="hidden" style="display: none"><pre>import Mathlib.Data.Nat.Factorial.Basic
