  </span><span class="tactic"><label for="tactic-state-7-5050-5071-13"><span class="keyword token" data-binding="kw-occ-Lean.Parser.Tactic.exact-5050" data-verso-hover="119">exact</span><span class="inter-text"> </span><span class="const anon-ctor token" data-binding="const-Exists.intro" data-verso-hover="120">⟨</span><span class="var token" data-binding="var-_uniq.59176.71" data-verso-hover="3">p</span><span class="const anon-ctor token" data-binding="const-Exists.intro" data-verso-hover="120">,</span><span class="inter-text"> </span><span class="var token" data-binding="var-_uniq.59176.249" data-verso-hover="107">np</span><span class="const anon-ctor token" data-binding="const-Exists.intro" data-verso-hover="120">,</span><span class="inter-text"> </span><span class="var token" data-binding="var-_uniq.59176.184" data-verso-hover="105">pp</span><span class="const anon-ctor token" data-binding="const-Exists.intro" data-verso-hover="120">⟩</span></label><input type="checkbox" class="tactic-toggle" id="tactic-state-7-5050-5071-13"/><span class="tactic-state">All goals completed! 🐙</span></span></code></div></div></div></div></div><aside class="lean-infoview" aria-label="Lean Infoview"><header><strong>Lean InfoView</strong></header><div class="lean-infoview-content" aria-live="polite"><p class="lean-infoview-empty">Click a tactic to see its goal.</p></div></aside></div></div></div></div></div></section><section class="organization-section" id="lean-fro" aria-label="The organization behind Lean"><div class="organization-inner container"><div class="organization-main"><div class="organization-intro reveal"><span class="organization-eyebrow">LEAN FRO</span><h2>The Organization Behind <span>Lean</span></h2><p class="organization-summary">Lean FRO supports the people, systems, documentation, automation, and community work that help Lean grow from a research tool into durable public infrastructure.</p><article class="organization-mission"><h3>A <span>focused</span> mission</h3><p>The Lean Focused Research Organization envisions a future where Lean drives innovation and progress across formal mathematics, software and hardware verification, and software development.</p><a href="/fro/roadmap">Read the roadmap →</a></article></div><div class="organization-history reveal transition-delay-small"><div class="organization-timeline" aria-label="Recent Lean milestones"><span class="organization-timeline-line" aria-hidden="true"></span><article class="organization-timeline-entry"><span class="organization-timeline-marker" aria-hidden="true"></span><div class="organization-timeline-card"><time class="organization-timeline-date">OCTOBER 2026</time><p>OpenAI <a href="https://openai.com/index/building-scientific-understanding-with-academic-communities/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">announces</a> a Lean-verified refutation of the Exponential Time Hypothesis and results on the Kakeya and Stein restriction conjectures, covered by <a href="https://www.newscientist.com/article/2596045-ai-refutes-30-year-old-mathematical-assumption-in-computer-science/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">New Scientist</a>; Axiom <a href="https://axiommath.ai/research/the-enormous-theorem-formalized/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">releases</a> the first complete <a href="https://cfsg.axiommath.ai/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Lean formalization</a> of the Classification of Finite Simple Groups; <a href="https://andtruth.com/press/andtruth-emerges-from-stealth/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">&amp;Truth</a> launches out of stealth with $70M in seed funding for Lean-based software verification, covered by <a href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/29/science/ai-eradicate-computer-bugs.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The New York Times</a>; Google DeepMind's <a href="https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/gemini-models/introducing-gemini-4-argon/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Gemini 4 Argon</a> and Anthropic's <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/research/designing-efficient-quantum-circuits" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Claude</a> design efficient quantum circuits, with key components verified in Lean; Google DeepMind <a href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2610.22603" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">publishes</a> a Gemini-based agentic pipeline for the Busy Beaver problem, integrating formal theorem proving in Lean</p></div></article><article class="organization-timeline-entry"><span class="organization-timeline-marker" aria-hidden="true"></span><div class="organization-timeline-card"><time class="organization-timeline-date">SEPTEMBER 2026</time><p>Anthropic <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/research/formalizing-fermats-last-theorem" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">announces</a> Lean formalization of Fermat's Last Theorem; OpenAI's <a href="https://openai.com/index/gpt-6-astra/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GPT-6 Astra</a> helped establish a stronger prime gap bound of 186, with <a href="https://github.com/openai/PrimeGaps186" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Lean formalization</a></p></div></article><article class="organization-timeline-entry"><span class="organization-timeline-marker" aria-hidden="true"></span><div class="organization-timeline-card"><time class="organization-timeline-date">AUGUST 2026</time><p>OpenAI provides <a href="https://github.com/openai/ten-proofs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Lean certificates</a> and <a href="https://openai.com/index/ten-advances-in-mathematics/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">announces progress</a> on 10 research-level mathematical problems; Anthropic <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/research/riemann-zeta" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">announces new results</a> related to the Riemann zeta function and provides <a href="https://github.com/anthropics/zeta-23-lean" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Lean formalizations</a> that pass Comparator validation; Lean FRO publishes <a href="https://lean-lang.org/fro/roadmap/y4-1/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Year 4 Part 1 Roadmap</a>; <a href="https://www.ibtimes.com/chris-hsu-how-one-programming-language-rewrote-mathematics-why-software-next-3806974" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">International Business Times</a> interviews Chris Hsu: 'How One Programming Language Rewrote Mathematics and Why Software Is Next'; Kim Morrison launches <a href="https://palomar-registry.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Palomar</a>, a Registry of Lean-Verified Mathematics</p></div></article><div class="organization-timeline-end"><a class="organization-timeline-more" href="/fro/about#a-brief-history-of-lean">See more<span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></div></div></div></div></section><section class="sponsors home-sponsors section-container reveal container" aria-label="Sponsors"><div class="heading-section"><span class="badge-primary">SPONSORS</span><h1 class="heading-title">Sponsors and Partners</h1><p class="heading-subtitle">Lean FRO gratefully acknowledges support from <b>Alex Gerko</b>, Founder and CEO of XTX Markets, as well as from the following organizations.</p></div><div class="sponsors-content"><a class="sponsor" href="https://www.sloan.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img src="/static/png/alfred.png" alt="Alfred P Sloan logo" class="sponsor-logo"/></a><a class="sponsor" href="https://www.convergentresearch.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img src="/static/png/convergent.png" alt="Convergent logo" class="sponsor-logo"/></a><div class="sponsor"><img src="/static/svg/merkin.svg" alt="Richard Merkin logo" class="sponsor-logo"/></div><a class="sponsor" href="https://www.simonsfoundation.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img src="/static/svg/simons.svg" alt="Simons logo" class="sponsor-logo"/></a><a class="sponsor" href="https://harmonic.fun/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img src="/static/svg/harmonic-logo.svg" alt="Harmonic logo" class="sponsor-logo"/></a><a class="sponsor" href="https://www.beneficialaifoundation.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img src="/static/svg/baif.svg" alt="BAIF logo" class="sponsor-logo"/></a><a class="sponsor" href="https://www.amazon.science/research-areas/automated-reasoning" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img src="/static/svg/amazon-light.svg" alt="Amazon Automated Reasoning logo" class="sponsor-logo sponsor-logo-light"/><img src="/static/svg/amazon-dark.svg" alt="Amazon Automated Reasoning logo" class="sponsor-logo sponsor-logo-dark"/></a></div></section><section class="cta" aria-label="Call to Action"><div class="cta-inner container"><div class="cta-card reveal"><div class="cta-topography" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="1497" height="853" viewBox="0 0 1497 853" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" alt="Topography background"><g clip-path="url(#clip0_1_2)"><path d="M963.26 588.384C965 594.558 972.76 601.055 980.21 604.545C989.53 608.911 1004.18 609.006 1016.59 608.745C1029.67 608.47 1040.87 607.285 1056.79 602.379C1082.79 594.367 1133.38 570.644 1154.99 556.061C1167.39 547.698 1175.18 540.644 1181.2 531.818C1186.35 524.281 1191.14 513.707 1190.72 507.576C1190.45 503.627 1188.55 500.807 1185.43 498.155C1180.62 494.066 1171.69 490.527 1161.31 489.367C1143.82 487.412 1112.99 492.016 1088.95 498.586C1063.15 505.637 1033.04 518.502 1011.81 531.818C994.25 542.837 975.52 558.027 968.35 569.474C964.16 576.154 961.68 582.738 963.26 588.384Z" stroke-opacity="0.7" stroke-linecap="round"></path><path d="M871.948 599.545C871.449 605.156 871.843 610.41 875.189 615.707C880.432 624.009 893.908 634.268 907.61 639.949C925.57 647.393 953.17 649.972 976.39 649.924C1000.21 649.875 1024.22 645.572 1048.75 639.124C1075.65 632.051 1104.09 620.594 1130.93 607.626C1158.85 594.136 1188.92 576.477 1212.91 559.141C1234.01 543.889 1256